<p>Holy hot dear mother of christ!</p>
<p>I'd like to applaud the level of polish on the advertisements and the audio logs. The former is well-constructed and vary wonderfully in composition, and do a great job for setting the tone for what will transpire; the latter are crisp, with one or two choice lines that *really* stand out in a good way.</p>
<p>Loved the pacing here as well, the way in which the investigation unfolds, the turn and reveal, kept me heavily immersed.</p>
<p>And. Fuck. What a wham line. There's something to be said for building a truly horrifying fate-worse-than-death in a place absolutely riddled with them. Excellent work.</p>

